  "narrative": {
    "intro": "AmerisourceBergen Drug obligated $6B in FY2026 to date through federal contracts. The company won 385,562 awards with an average award size of $15.5K. Obligations are down 19.9% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows obligations of $2.1B in FY21, $2B in FY22, $4.4B in FY23, $6.1B in FY24, and $7.4B in FY25. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $6B in the current fiscal year to date. Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing is the largest NAICS market for AmerisourceBergen Drug with $4B, followed by Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers at $2B and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing at $639K. Current-year totals are partial and reported as fiscal year to date. Award-value totals in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than obligations.",
